@startuml
title bloc_bridge - message lifecycle and shutdown
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Telegram user" as user
participant "Telegram API" as tg
participant "Main thread\nbridge.main + bridge_runtime" as main
participant "Polling thread\ntelegram.polling + handle_update" as poll
queue "Request queue" as tasks
participant "Request worker\nbridge._request_worker" as worker
participant "OpenCode exchange\nopencode.exchange" as exchange
database "Session mapping + request metadata\nSQLite and JSON in volume" as state
participant "OpenCode API\nvia opencode.api" as oc
participant "Event watcher\nDaemon thread" as events
participant "Opper API\noptional, no credentials" as opper

note over poll,oc
  Network calls use http_api; Telegram replies use telegram.markdown_renderer.
  Startup loads the session mapping, acquires the polling lock, and recovers durable requests.
end note
note over worker,exchange
  bridge.py routes requests and owns Telegram presentation.
  opencode.exchange owns OpenCode submission, monitoring, correlation, and recovery.
end note
main -> poll : Start single daemon poller
user -> tg : Send message
poll -> tg : getUpdates(offset, timeout=50)
tg --> poll : Updates

alt Empty/non-text message or chat not allowed
    poll -> poll : Ignore update; log rejected chat if applicable
else Allowed text message
    alt /status or /cancel
        poll -> state : Check request reference and chat ownership
        opt /cancel for submitted request
            poll -> oc : POST /session/{id}/abort
            oc --> poll : Abort accepted / not confirmed
        end
        poll -> tg : Send sanitized status or cancellation feedback
    else Another request is active in this chat
        poll -> tg : Refuse new prompt; include active reference and control commands
    else New request
        poll -> state : Insert request row keyed by reference and Telegram update_id
        poll -> tg : sendMessage("Request received. Ref: ...")
        tg --> poll : Acknowledgement message_id
        poll -> state : Persist acknowledgement message_id
        alt No usable acknowledgement
            poll -> state : Mark acknowledgement delivery unknown; do not submit
        else Request capacity reached
            poll -> state : Mark request rejected
            poll -> tg : Edit acknowledgement: bridge busy
        else Capacity available
            poll -> tasks : Enqueue request (32 admitted maximum)
            tasks -> worker : One of 4 daemon workers
            worker -> worker : Acquire per-chat lock
            alt Slash command other than /status or /cancel
                worker -> worker : Route /start, /help or unknown command locally
                opt /new, /health or /cost
                    worker -> oc : Session creation, health or history API
                    oc --> worker : API result (no model prompt)
                    opt /new
                        worker -> state : Persist selected session
                    end
                    opt /health and TELEGRAM_HEALTH_OPPER_ENABLED=true
                        worker -> opper : GET /v3/compat/models (5 s socket timeout)
                        opper --> worker : Reachability only; no inference
                    end
                end
            else Regular prompt
                worker -> exchange : Submit or resume exchange
                opt No session for this chat
                    exchange -> oc : POST /api/session
                    oc --> exchange : Session ID
                    exchange -> oc : PUT /api/experimental/session/{id}/instructions/entries/bloc-telegram
                    oc --> exchange : Telegram instructions attached to session
                    exchange -> state : Persist chat-to-session mapping
                end
                exchange -> oc : Read session tree history (cost baseline)
                exchange -> state : Persist session ID and generated prompt message ID
                exchange -> events : Start SSE watcher for this exchange
                events -> oc : GET /api/event
                exchange -> oc : POST /api/session/{id}/prompt
                oc --> exchange : Submission accepted
                exchange -> state : Mark request running
                loop Until correlated completion and two idle samples, or 5 days maximum
                    exchange -> oc : GET /api/session/active (10 s HTTP timeout)
                    oc --> exchange : Running sessions; absent sessions are idle
                    exchange -> oc : GET /api/session/{id}/message (10 s HTTP timeout)
                    oc --> exchange : Paginated v2 message history; normalize and correlate by prompt ID
                    opt Transient HTTP timeout
                        exchange -> exchange : Retry status/history; keep request active
                    end
                    opt Correlated reasoning/tool event available
                        oc --> events : SSE event
                        events -> exchange : Bounded event queue (128)
                        exchange -> exchange : Select deterministic safe stage and tool label
                    end
                    opt OpenCode has reported correlated usage
                        exchange -> exchange : Recompute partial cost from assistant history
                        exchange -> worker : Invoke progress callback
                        worker -> tg : Edit progress with observed cost, controls, and reference
                    end
                    opt Assistant error in correlated history outside a stop request
                        exchange -> exchange : Fail promptly with sanitized status + reference
                    end
                    opt First progress event or 30 s since last progress
                        exchange -> worker : Invoke progress callback
                        worker -> tg : Edit acknowledgement with safe progress
                    end
                end
                opt User cancellation or 5 days limit
                    exchange -> oc : POST /api/session/{id}/interrupt
                    oc --> exchange : Abort result
                    exchange -> exchange : Keep chat active until OpenCode is confirmed idle
                end
                exchange -> oc : Read session tree history
                exchange -> exchange : Build response + cost and tool-name footers
                exchange -> events : Set watcher stop event
                exchange --> worker : Return final response
            end
            worker -> state : Mark delivery pending
            worker -> tg : Edit acknowledgement with final response
            worker -> state : Mark terminal state
        end
    end
end
poll -> poll : Advance offset after handling the update

== Shutdown can happen during any of the above steps ==
main -> main : Receive SIGTERM / SIGINT; set shared stop event
note over main,events
  No new updates are dispatched once shutdown is observed.
  Cooperative checks prevent further work after blocked HTTP calls return.
  Running sockets need not return: polling, request and SSE threads are daemon threads.
  The supervisor joins the polling thread for at most 0.2 s, then main cleans up and exits.
  Queued but unsubmitted work is marked interrupted on restart, never replayed.
  Submitted work is recovered by session/prompt message IDs and monitored without resubmission.
  Ambiguous delivery or OpenCode state is exposed through /status; work is never replayed blindly.
end note
main -> main : Release polling lock; restore signal handlers; exit
@enduml
